<h2>Where should the filters go on Account activity?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Three placements for the same controls (event type, plus a shortcut for failed sign-ins). Click one, then reply in the terminal.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar above the table</h3>
      <p>Always visible between the intro and the table. Nothing hidden behind a click; costs one row of vertical space.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;font-size:13px">Event type
              <select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option></select></label>
            <label style="font-size:13px"><input type="checkbox"> Failed sign-ins only</label>
            <button class="mock-button">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:13px">Showing 12 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick-filter chips above the table</h3>
      <p>One-click presets (All, Failed sign-ins, Sign-ins, Account changes). Fast for the common case; grouping types into chips means choosing the groups.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
            <button class="mock-button">All</button>
            <button class="mock-button" style="opacity:.6">Failed sign-ins</button>
            <button class="mock-button" style="opacity:.6">Sign-ins and sign-outs</button>
            <button class="mock-button" style="opacity:.6">Account changes</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:13px">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button with a popover</h3>
      <p>Compact; room to grow later. Filters are hidden until opened, so the failed sign-in shortcut is one click further away.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px">
            <p style="margin:0">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;width:240px;margin:0 0 8px auto;font-size:13px">
            Event type: [All events]<br>
            [ ] Failed sign-ins only<br>
            <em>Apply / Clear</em>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
